tton>\n125:   </div>\n126:   <p id=\"status-msg\" style=\"margin:12px 0 0;font-weight:600\"></p>\n127: </div>\n128: \n129: <div id=\"questions-container\"></div>\n130: \n131: <div class=\"floating-add\">\n132:   <button id=\"add-q-btn\" class=\"plus-btn\" type=\"button\">+ Add Question</button>\n133: </div>\n134: \n135: </div>\n136: \n137: <script src=\"https://www.gstatic.com/firebasejs/10.14.0/firebase-app-compat.js\"></script>\n138: <script src=\"https://www.gstatic.com/firebasejs/10.14.0/firebase-firestore-compat.js\"></script>\n139: <script>\n140: const cfg = {"}
{"step_index":644,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-08T22:47:42Z","input_tokens":2413,"cache_read_tokens":150564,"output_tokens":656,"thinking":"The UI for `teacher.html` currently features a tab bar within a `.wrap` container. This tab bar includes buttons for \"Quiz Editor\" and \"Submissions\", designed with a clean tab style. A CSS class `.tab-nav` provides styling options resembling modern segmented or pill tabs.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"search_web","args":{"query":"quiz builder teacher dashboard tabs submissions questions ui design patterns"}}]}
{"step_index":645,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-08T22:47:51Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-09T06:47:51+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-09T06:47:56+08:00\nThe search for \"quiz builder teacher dashboard tabs submissions questions ui design patterns\" returned the following summary:\nDesigning a **Teacher Dashboard** featuring a **Quiz Builder**, **Questions management**, and **Student Submissions** requires balancing heavy data density with low-friction creation tools. \n\nThe best UI/UX design patterns for structuring these elements focus on reducing cognitive load for educators who frequently bounce between authoring content and grading student outcomes.\n\n---\n\n### 1. High-Level Architecture & Dashboard Tabs Pattern\nThe top-level navigation should use horizontal tabs or a segmented controller to clearly divide the lifecycle of an assessment (Creation vs. Evaluation).\n\n*   **Suggested Tab Structure:**\n    1.  **Overview / Analytics:** Quick metrics (Completion rate, average score, hardest question).\n    2.  **Builder / Questions:** The workspace for authoring and arranging test items[1].\n    3.  **Settings:** Timing, availability windows, security (proctoring/randomization), and grading weights.\n    4.  **Submissions / Grading:** The central hub for reviewing student attempts[1].\n*   **UI Pattern Tip:** Keep a persistent **Primary Action Bar** sticky at the top or bottom right containing high-stakes actions like *“Preview”*, *“Discard Changes”*, and *“Publish / Assign”*[1].\n\n---\n\n### 2. The Quiz Builder & Questions Tab UI Patterns\nWhen a teacher clicks into the **Questions** tab, they need an interface that handles both macro-organization (the flow of the test) and micro-details (the individual question configurations).\n\n*   **Split-Panel Layout (The Master-Detail Pattern):**\n    *   *Left Sidebar (Navigation/Outline):* A compact, drag-and-drop list of question blocks (e.g., *Q1: Multiple Choice, Q2: Short Answer, Q3: Hotspot*[2]). Shows quick status icons (e.g., points allocated, validation errors like missing correct answers).\n    *   *Main Canvas (Editor):* Focuses on the selected question item. Changes made here instantly update the left outline.\n*   **Accordion vs. Card Stack Pattern:**\n    *   For shorter quizzes, use an expandable **Card Stack** where all questions live on one scrollable page, but individual questions can be collapsed to minimize scrolling fatigue.\n*   **Inline Question Type Switcher:**\n    *   A dropdown or icon-pill selector near the top of the question card allowing teachers to switch question formats (MCQ, True/False, Matching, Essay) without losing typed prompt text.\n*   **Empty & Error States:**\n    *   If a question lacks a designated \"correct answer\" or has zero points, highlight the specific field with a soft inline banner (e.g., *“Select at least one correct option to publish”*) rather than blocking the entire interface silently[1].\n\n---\n\n### 3. Submissions & Grading Tab UI Patterns\nThe Submissions tab bridges the gap between completed student work and performance tracking. It usually requires a dual approach: **Aggregated Data** (spreadsheet style) and **Individual Evaluation** (focus mode).\n\n*   **Master-Detail Table/List View (Triage View):**\n    *   A robust data table listing students (`Name`, `Submission Status`, `Submitted Time`, `Score`, `Actions`).\n    *   *Badges & Color Coding:* Quick visual indicators for status—e.g., *Needs Grading* (Amber/Yellow), *Graded* (Green), *Late / Missing* (Red/Gray).\n    *   *Filter & Sort Toolbar:* Quick filters like \"Show items needing manual review\" vs. \"Auto-graded only.\"\n*   **Split-Screen \"SpeedGrader\" Pattern:**\n    *   When a teacher clicks a student's submission, avoid forcing them to navigate back and forth. Open a **Slide-over Drawer** or a dedicated **Split View**:\n        *   *Left Side:* The student’s complete quiz layout with their answers highlighted alongside correct answers.\n        *   *Right Side:* A persistent grading panel with input fields for points per question, quick comment macros (canned feedback snippets), and an overall comment box.\n    *   *Keyboard Shortcuts:* Implement hotkeys (`Enter` to save and jump to the next student, arrow keys to navigate questions) to dramatically speed up bulk grading.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Key UI/UX Micro-Patterns to Incorporate\n\n*   **Contextual Drag Handles:** Use standard 6-dot grip icons on the left of question items to signify that reordering via drag-and-drop is supported.\n*   **Live Preview Toggle:** A prominent toggle switch or modal button (*\"Preview as Student\"*) so teachers can test interactive elements, randomized question pools, and timers before deploying[1].\n*   **Auto-Save Indication:** Because quiz building involves heavy content entry, always display a subtle, non-intrusive status indicator in the header (e.g., *“All changes saved to draft”* or *“Saving…”*) to alleviate user anxiety.\n\nSources:\n[1] [figr.design](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGZ3uIGnHB1N0B7ytTqQeq_OEihnG-zmhx4Lo4OTb1MjraPK0NMSN-iYnF_h9W5xNGSCF1mR8UsT0kbHWV8SgnhmSr5DLOGskqMmSUIe6DNSkCfSHxmh5DBhTcrVe1K9P0=)\n[2] [dribbble.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEly5QaJ3IlHdOCrhUHyr6U9q9UlE7jpRC380Tn_bFIRAXiKMXt34oofwY87FzArfkYJoOnjcMlmuXmRIJLxLnQkxYG7sh20WxegQ8JqH1p3SeCWNyD0natVa1IF9I5)\n\nNote: Source URLs are HTTP redirects; check where they resolve if you need the direct link."}
{"step_index":646,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-08T22:47:57Z","input_tokens":2075,"cache_read_tokens":152984,"output_tokens":2143,"thinking":"I'm thinking through how to approach this.\n\n\nThe initial structure shows two tabs: \"Quiz Editor\" and \"Submissions\", with corresponding view containers. The \"Submissions\" tab contains a badge and a container to display submission data, initially showing \"No submissions recorded yet.\" Tab click handlers are implemented to toggle visibility and active states.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":true,"Summary":"Implementation plan to add a top tab navigation bar in teacher.html with 'Quiz Editor' and 'Submissions' tabs to view who has completed the quiz.","UserFacing":true},"Content":"# Implementation Plan: Add Submissions Tab in Teacher Portal\n\n## 1. Overview of Requested Changes\n\n- **Target**: [teacher.html](file:///c:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/teacher.html).\n- **Goal**: Introduce a segmented tab navigation bar at the top of the teacher portal with two views:\n  1. **Quiz Editor**: The existing quiz authoring, question management, and configuration workspace.\n  2. **Submissions**: A dedicated view to track and display students who have completed and submitted their quiz.\n- **Naming**: The tab is named **Submissions** (with the view header labeled **Completed Students**), matching industry standard LMS terminology and the underlying Firestore collection name (`submissions`).\n\n---\n\n## 2. Technical Implementation Details\n\n### 2.1 [teacher.html](file:///c:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/teacher.html)\n- **Styling**:\n  Add clean segmented tab bar styles to the `<style>` block:\n  ```css\n  .tab-nav{display:flex;gap:8px;margin-bottom:14px;background:var(--card);border:1px solid var(--bd);border-radius:12px;padding:6px}\n  .tab-item{flex:1;padding:10px 14px;border:none;border-radius:8px;background:transparent;color:var(--mu);font-weight:600;font-size:0.95rem;cursor:pointer;transition:all .15s ease}\n  .tab-item.active{background:var(--pr);color:#fff}\n  ```\n- **Markup**:\n  - Add `<nav class=\"tab-nav\">` with `#tab-btn-editor` and `#tab-btn-sub`.\n  - Wrap existing editor cards, questions list, and floating add button in `<div id=\"view-editor\">`.\n  - Add `<div id=\"view-sub\" class=\"hide\">` containing a card with header `Completed Students`, submission counter badge, and `#sub-container` placeholder.\n- **Behavior**:\n  - Add click handlers for `#tab-btn-editor` and `#tab-btn-sub` to toggle visibility between `#view-editor` and `#view-sub` and toggle `.active` classes.\n\n### 2.2 [HISTORY.md](file:///c:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/HISTORY.md)\n- Append Non-Major Patch 1.0.15 documenting the top tab navigation bar and the new Submissions view placeholder per Rule 1.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Dependency & Ripple Effect Analysis\n\n| Component / Flow | Dependency Type | Potential Risk | Mitigation |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Quiz Editor Workspace | Encapsulated in `#view-editor` | Broken selectors or card references | All existing IDs (`qtitle`, `qdesc`, `save-btn`, `dl-quiz-btn`, `questions-container`, `add-q-btn`) remain unmodified. |\n| Floating Add Button (`.floating-add`) | Child of `#view-editor` | Visible when switching to Submissions | Grouped inside `#view-editor` so it automatically hides when viewing Submissions. |\n| Side Edge Panel (`#options-panel`) | Global overlay | Drawer z-index or trigger issues | Floating gear icon button (`#opt-btn`) and slide-out panel remain global, accessible across both tabs. |\n| Original File (`QUIZ06 (1) (1).html`) | Untouchable asset | Rule violation | Untouched per Rules 2 & 12. |\n\n---\n\n## 4. Verification Plan (Rules 3 & 10)\n\n1. **Tab Navigation Verification**:\n   - Verify `#tab-btn-editor` and `#tab-btn-sub` are rendered.\n   - Verify clicking **Submissions** hides `#view-editor` and reveals `#view-sub`.\n   - Verify clicking **Quiz Editor** hides `#view-sub` and restores `#view-editor`.\n2. **Editor Integrity Verification**:\n   - Verify question card adding, editing, title/description inputs, and save buttons remain fully functional.\n3. **Rule 9 Zero-Comment Compliance**:\n   - Verify zero comments or docstrings in `teacher.html`.\n4. **Original File Integrity**:\n   - Confirm `QUIZ06 (1) (1).html` remains untouched.\n","Overwrite":true,"Path":"C:\\Users\\CxAdmin\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\8f2bd4b5-d81b-4839-aa40-a5c3a5acaa6a\\implementation_plan.md"}}]}
